# Chroma library, modern Earth: THE WORLD ANSWERS, writer 2 (chroma-world/spheres/world-answers-v1.md, 10-19; read
# only with the Engine's world_answers switch on). Spheres comm (shops, markets, banks), prod (works, farms,
# workshops) and learn (schools, colleges, libraries).
#   E4 the sphere asks: asked_help (rung 2), asked_lead (rung 3), asked_speak (rung 4), one of each a sphere; {place}
#      is the place in that sphere. Everyday layout: five one-colour ways and one cross cycle; lever: on every option
#      (loyalty or lead a yes, voice a yes in their own way or a bargain, exit or neglect a no).
#   F2 decisions for others (Known lives): four a sphere, 2 to 4 directions each with scope:. Leading colours over
#      all twelve: 35 one-colour options (7 a colour) and one cross cycle (W>U U>B B>R R>G G>W), so each colour leads
#      8 times by first letter and 8 by the checker's split count.

# ================================================================ E4 the sphere asks: comm

== the traders ask for spring fair Saturdays
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 20-85
calls: WG
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: months
roles: colleague, neighbour, friend
cast_want: asked_help
sphere: comm
earth: the traders at the market you know ask if you could give some Saturdays to help run their spring fair
scene: {N} has been coming to {place} long enough that the traders know {N} by name. One morning the woman who keeps the traders' ledger stops by with a clipboard. The spring fair needs hands on Saturdays: setting out the trestles, minding the cash tin, sorting the pitches. Only a few weekends, she says, and they thought of {N} first.
scene W: A fair that runs on goodwill needs someone who turns up when the rota says so, and {N} is known for turning up.
scene G: These are the same faces {N} has bought bread and onions from for years; saying yes would make {N} one of them.
- W | sign up for every Saturday on the rota and keep the cash tin honest | lever: loyalty | v: conformity, benevolence | foot: place comm.market | chance: 80
- U | offer to redraw the pitch plan so the fair runs smoother than last year | lever: voice | v: achievement, self-direction | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- B | agree to help, in return for a better pitch next season | lever: voice | v: power, achievement | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 75
- R | say yes on the spot and talk two friends into coming along | lever: loyalty | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: place comm.market; person friend | chance: 80
- G | help the old way: bring the tea urn and stay to pack up at dusk | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: person neighbour | chance: 85
- W>G | take on keeping the fair's long-standing rules, the same for every stall | lever: lead | v: conformity, tradition | foot: place comm.market | chance: 70
- U>W | give one Saturday and write down how the day should run, for whoever comes next | lever: loyalty | v: universalism, achievement | foot: person colleague | chance: 80
- B>U | keep the Saturdays free, but offer an evening on the traders' accounts | lever: voice | v: power, achievement | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 80
- R>B | say no warmly: Saturday is the one free day, and it stays free | lever: exit | v: hedonism, self-direction | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 85
- G>R | keep Saturdays for the family, and promise to come to the fair to cheer | lever: neglect | v: tradition, hedonism | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 85
works: The fair runs on time that spring, and the traders at {place} start keeping a cup of tea back for {N} on Saturdays.
works: Whatever {N} gave or held back, it was said plainly, and the traders take it well.
fails: The Saturday rota falls apart by midsummer, and the clipboard comes round again, with more pleading in it.
fails: A couple of the old traders take the answer badly, and for a while the greetings at {place} are a little cooler.

== the shop committee wants a new chair
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-85
calls: WB
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: years
roles: colleague, elder, friend, rival
cast_want: asked_lead
sphere: comm
earth: the committee that runs a shop you know well asks you to take the chair
scene: The committee that runs {place} has lost its chair, and at the end of a long meeting {colleague} turns to {N}. Everyone at {place} knows {N}: the hours put in, the sense {N} talks at meetings, the way the younger staff come to {N} with questions. The committee would like {N} to take it on, {colleague} says, starting next month.
scene W: A shop held in common needs someone who will keep the books straight and the meetings fair.
scene B: The chair decides who is hired, what is stocked and what is paid; it is a real post, with real weight.
- W | take the chair, and start by writing down how decisions get made | lever: lead | v: conformity, universalism | foot: place comm.shop | chance: 70
- U | take it for a trial year, after going through the old accounts with the last chair | lever: lead | v: achievement, self-direction | foot: person mentor | chance: 70
- B | accept, on condition the chair has the final say over hiring | lever: lead | v: power | foot: person rival | chance: 65
- R | turn it down: running a committee would take the joy out of the place | lever: exit | v: hedonism, stimulation | foot: means freedom+.04 | chance: 85
- G | say the shop has older hands, and back one of them for the chair | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: person elder | chance: 80
- W>B | take the chair and set firm targets for each quarter | lever: lead | v: achievement, conformity | foot: place comm.shop | chance: 65
- U>R | offer to train the new staff, and leave the chair to someone else | lever: loyalty | v: self-direction, stimulation | foot: person colleague | chance: 80
- B>G | accept, and give the friends who backed the move a seat at the table | lever: lead | v: power, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 70
- R>W | accept with a rush of ideas, and promise every member a fair say | lever: lead | v: stimulation, universalism | foot: means time-.06 | chance: 60
- G>U | keep to the counter as before, and learn the trade properly first | lever: neglect | v: tradition, self-direction | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 85
works: By the next spring the committee at {place} runs more smoothly, and the staff speak of how things are done now without thinking about it.
works: {colleague} says afterwards that {N} answered the way {N} does everything, and that it was the right answer for {place}.
fails: The first months are rough, and a decision has to be undone in front of the whole committee.
fails: Somebody at {place} decides they liked it better before, and says so, often, where the rest can hear.

== the traders want a voice at the council
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-90
calls: WR
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: years
roles: colleague, elder, rival, friend
cast_want: asked_speak
sphere: comm
earth: the council wants someone from the market to speak for the traders, and they have asked you
scene: The council is about to decide the market square's future: the rents, the parking, whether the weekday market stays at all. The traders of {place} meet in the back of the café and argue for an hour. In the end they agree on one thing: {N} should speak for them. {N} has stood at {place} longer than most, and people listen when {N} talks.
scene W: The traders do not all want the same thing, and whoever speaks owes each of them a fair hearing first.
scene R: The square is where half the town meets on a weekday, and {N} can feel how much it would hurt to lose it.
- W | agree, and gather every trader's view before writing a word | lever: lead | v: universalism, conformity | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 70
- U | agree, and come armed with the figures: footfall, takings, what the town would lose | lever: voice | v: achievement | foot: person colleague | chance: 65
- B | say no: speaking for everyone means answering to everyone | lever: exit | v: self-direction, power | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 85
- R | speak, and speak from the heart about what the square means to those who come | lever: voice | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: place rule.voice | chance: 65
- G | say the oldest trader should speak, and stand beside her | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: person elder | chance: 80
- W>R | set out the rules the traders agreed, then rally the crowd in the gallery | lever: lead | v: universalism, stimulation | foot: place rule.voice | chance: 60
- U>G | agree, and tell the council the square's long history from the old records | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, achievement | foot: place learn.keeping | chance: 70
- B>W | agree, in return for a seat on the market committee afterwards | lever: voice | v: power, conformity | foot: door kept your word | chance: 70
- R>U | leave the speech to another, but spend the evenings helping find the words | lever: loyalty | v: benevolence, self-direction | foot: person friend | chance: 80
- G>B | keep to the stall that day: the takings will not wait | lever: neglect | v: security, tradition | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 85
works: The council hears the traders out, and the weekday market keeps its place in the square for now.
works: Afterwards the traders at {place} stand {N} a drink and go over the meeting again, line by line.
fails: The council decides much as it meant to, and the traders grumble that nobody could have changed its mind.
fails: Not every trader liked how it went, and one of them makes sure {N} hears about it for weeks.

# ================================================================ E4 the sphere asks: prod

== the growers call for harvest weekends
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 20-85
calls: GW
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: months
roles: colleague, neighbour, friend
cast_want: asked_help
sphere: prod
earth: the farm you work near asks if you could help bring in the harvest at the weekends
scene: Harvest comes early at {place} this year, and rain is forecast for the week after. {colleague} rings on a Thursday night: could {N} give the next three weekends, early starts, to help bring it in? There is no pay to speak of, only the meals at the long table and a box of whatever is picked.
scene G: The fields have been worked this way for longer than anyone can remember, every hand the town can spare at the end of summer.
scene W: The crop belongs to everyone who put work into it, and it will not wait for anyone's convenience.
- W | sign up for all three weekends, the earliest shift, without being asked twice | lever: loyalty | v: conformity, benevolence | foot: place prod.land | chance: 80
- U | come, and work out a better order for the fields so the crews waste less time | lever: voice | v: achievement, self-direction | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- B | agree to come, for a share of the crop to sell on | lever: voice | v: power, achievement | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 75
- R | turn up with music and a crowd of friends, and make a party of the picking | lever: loyalty | v: hedonism, stimulation | foot: person friend | chance: 75
- G | come every weekend, and stay for the meal at the long table afterwards | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: place prod.land; person neighbour | chance: 85
- W>U | come, and keep a proper record of what each field gave, for next year | lever: loyalty | v: conformity, achievement | foot: place prod.land | chance: 75
- U>B | give one weekend and spend it learning the machines, a skill worth having | lever: voice | v: self-direction, achievement | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 70
- B>R | decline, and keep the weekends for the trip already planned | lever: exit | v: hedonism, self-direction | foot: means freedom+.03 | chance: 85
- R>G | stay out of the fields, but bake for the crews and bring it out at noon | lever: loyalty | v: benevolence, hedonism | foot: person neighbour | chance: 85
- G>W | decline honestly: the household needs those weekends | lever: neglect | v: tradition, security | foot: means ties+.03 | chance: 85
works: The last cart comes in the day before the rain, and {place} keeps a place at the long table for {N} after that.
works: However {N} answered, it was taken as meant, and {colleague} says so when they next meet.
fails: The crews run short on the second weekend, and half the low field is lost to the rain.
fails: The answer lands badly with one or two at {place}, and it takes a season for the coolness to pass.

== the workshop needs a teacher for its apprentices
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-85
calls: UG
tone: mixed
life: work
horizon: years
roles: boss, colleague, mentor
cast_want: asked_lead
sphere: prod
earth: the workshop where you work asks you to take on the apprentices
scene: The old foreman at {place} is retiring at last, and the three apprentices need someone to teach them. {boss} has asked around, and every answer came back with the same name. {N} has the hands for the work and, it seems, the patience.
scene U: Teaching a craft means knowing it well enough to say why each step is done, and {N} wonders whether {N} does.
scene G: The trade came to {N} from the old foreman, who had it from someone before him; now it is {Ns} turn to pass it on.
- W | take them on, with a set plan of what each must learn by the year's end | lever: lead | v: conformity, achievement | foot: place prod.craft | chance: 70
- U | take them on, and teach the why of each step, not only the how | lever: lead | v: self-direction, universalism | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- B | agree, for a foreman's pay and a foreman's title | lever: lead | v: power, achievement | foot: means money+.05 | chance: 65
- R | turn it down and stay at the bench, where the joy of the work is | lever: exit | v: hedonism, self-direction | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 85
- G | take them on the old foreman's way: side by side, one task at a time | lever: lead | v: tradition | foot: person mentor | chance: 75
- W>R | take them on, with clear rules and a prize for the year's best piece | lever: lead | v: conformity, stimulation | foot: place prod.craft | chance: 70
- U>G | teach them the old skills, and write each one down before it is lost | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, achievement | foot: place learn.keeping | chance: 70
- B>W | agree, if the workshop sets fair pay for the extra hours for everyone who teaches | lever: voice | v: power, universalism | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 65
- R>U | leave the post to another, but show them the tricks no book has, on Fridays | lever: loyalty | v: stimulation, self-direction | foot: person colleague | chance: 80
- G>B | decline: the household's own business needs those hours | lever: exit | v: security, tradition | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 85
works: By the spring the apprentices at {place} work with a care the old hands recognise, and {boss} notices.
works: {N} answers in {Ns} own way, and the workshop finds a way to work with it.
fails: The first months are hard on everyone, and one of the apprentices nearly gives up the trade.
fails: {boss} had hoped for a different answer, and the workshop's welcome is a little stiffer for a while.

== the valley asks for someone to speak for its fields
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-90
calls: RG
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: years
roles: colleague, neighbour, rival, friend
cast_want: asked_speak
sphere: prod
earth: the growers and the people who work the land near you want you to speak for them at the town hall
scene: The town is deciding where the new houses will go, and the plan on the table takes the fields behind {place}. The growers and the people who work there have met twice in the barn. At the second meeting someone says what most of them were thinking: {N} should speak for them. {N} knows the place, and {N} is trusted.
scene R: {N} has spent years with hands in that soil, and the thought of it under tarmac makes {Ns} chest tight.
scene G: Some of these families have worked the same fields for generations, and they want one of their own to stand up.
- W | agree, and set out the growers' case point by point, with what the rules allow | lever: lead | v: conformity, universalism | foot: place rule.counsel | chance: 65
- U | agree, and bring the soil surveys and the yields of the last twenty seasons | lever: voice | v: achievement | foot: person colleague | chance: 65
- B | agree, and quietly look for a deal that pays the growers well to move | lever: voice | v: power, security | foot: person rival | chance: 65
- R | agree, and speak with all the fire of someone whose hands are in that soil | lever: lead | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: place rule.voice | chance: 60
- G | agree, and bring the families who farmed there for generations to stand behind | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: place prod.land | chance: 70
- W>B | agree, and ask that the growers' own committee be written into the plan | lever: voice | v: conformity, power | foot: door kept your word | chance: 65
- U>R | leave the stand to another, but write the speech for whoever gives it | lever: loyalty | v: self-direction, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 80
- B>G | speak only for the families nearest the fields, whose case is strongest | lever: voice | v: power, benevolence | foot: person neighbour | chance: 70
- R>W | say no: feelings run too high, and the case needs a cooler voice | lever: exit | v: universalism, security | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 85
- G>U | decline, and lend the old field books to whoever does speak | lever: exit | v: tradition, security | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 85
works: The council sends the plan back to be redrawn, and the fields behind {place} are left alone for now.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the growers at {place} say it was an honest answer, and they remember it.
fails: The plan goes through with a few changes, and the growers at {place} start talking about where they will go.
fails: A few in the barn think {N} let them down, and they say so at the next meeting.

