== the homework club needs Tuesday helpers
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 20-85
calls: UG
tone: mixed
life: community, learning
horizon: months
roles: colleague, neighbour, friend
cast_want: asked_help
sphere: learn
earth: the library you know asks if you could give an evening a week to its homework club
scene: {place} has run a homework club on Tuesday evenings for years, and this term two of its helpers have moved away. A note goes round, and then {colleague} asks {N} directly: one evening a week, sitting with whoever needs a hand with sums or spelling or a letter to the council.
scene U: {N} likes explaining things, and it has been a while since anyone asked {N} to.
scene G: Someone sat with {N} like this once, long ago, and it made all the difference.
- W | take a regular Tuesday and never miss one | lever: loyalty | v: conformity, benevolence | foot: place learn.keeping | chance: 85
- U | come, and bring a box of old workbooks sorted by level | lever: loyalty | v: universalism, achievement | foot: person colleague | chance: 80
- B | agree, in return for a good reference from the head librarian | lever: voice | v: achievement, power | foot: person patron | chance: 75
- R | come once, have such a good evening that it turns into every week | lever: loyalty | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 80
- G | help the way the old librarian once helped: patiently, one person at a time | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: place learn.keeping | chance: 80
- W>B | run the sign-in sheet and the rota, so the club can apply for a grant | lever: lead | v: conformity, achievement | foot: means time-.04 | chance: 70
- U>R | skip the Tuesdays, but record short lessons the club can play any time | lever: voice | v: self-direction, stimulation | foot: lesson help can come from afar | chance: 75
- B>G | decline: the evenings go to the second job that keeps the household going | lever: exit | v: security, achievement | foot: means money+.03 | chance: 85
- R>W | jump in with enthusiasm, then settle on a fixed night once the term starts | lever: loyalty | v: stimulation, conformity | foot: door kept your word | chance: 70
- G>U | decline for now, and send them a retired teacher from down the street | lever: neglect | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 85
works: By the end of term the Tuesday room at {place} is full, and {colleague} thanks {N} by name in the newsletter.
works: The answer was honest, and the people at {place} think no less of {N} for it.
fails: The club limps on short of hands, and {colleague} looks tired every time {N} passes the desk.
fails: Some at {place} had hoped for more, and for a while the welcome there is polite rather than warm.

== the college asks for an evening teacher
tier: everyday
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-85
calls: UB
tone: mixed
life: work, learning
horizon: years
roles: boss, colleague, friend
cast_want: asked_lead
sphere: learn
earth: the college you know asks you to teach an evening class in what you know best
scene: The adult classes at {place} have lost their teacher for the spring term, and {boss} has heard that {N} knows the subject better than anyone in town. The pay is small, the room is cold, and the students range from school-leavers to pensioners. Would {N} take it on?
scene U: There is a way of teaching this that nobody has tried here, and {N} has thought about it for years.
scene B: A class of one's own is a foot in the door, and doors at {place} do not open often.
- W | take the class, with a syllabus, a register and a fair test at the end | lever: lead | v: conformity, universalism | foot: place learn.higher | chance: 70
- U | take it, and rebuild the course from the ground up | lever: lead | v: self-direction, achievement | foot: person colleague | chance: 65
- B | take it as a step toward a proper post on the staff | lever: lead | v: achievement, power | foot: person boss | chance: 70
- R | take it, and make the cold room the liveliest evening in town | lever: lead | v: stimulation, hedonism | foot: person friend | chance: 65
- G | suggest the retired teacher, and offer to sit in as her helper | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: person teacher | chance: 80
- W>U | take it for one term only, and leave notes so the next teacher starts well | lever: loyalty | v: conformity, achievement | foot: door kept your word | chance: 80
- U>B | decline: the private study takes every spare hour, and this would slow it | lever: exit | v: achievement, self-direction | foot: door turned down a chance | chance: 85
- B>R | agree, if the hours can bend around everything else | lever: voice | v: self-direction, power | foot: means time-.03 | chance: 70
- R>G | say no for now: this season belongs to friends and home | lever: neglect | v: hedonism, benevolence | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 85
- G>W | take it on as a debt repaid to the town that taught the trade | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, universalism | foot: place learn.higher | chance: 75
works: By the last evening of term nobody misses a class, and {boss} asks whether {N} would think about the autumn.
works: {N} gave {boss} a clear answer, and {boss} respects it more than a half-hearted yes.
fails: The class thins out by the fourth week, and the cold room feels colder for the empty chairs.
fails: The answer leaves {boss} in a bind, and it is a while before {place} asks {N} for anything again.

