== the market square's trading hours
tier: decision
cast_want: decide
sphere: comm
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-90
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: years
roles: colleague, neighbour, rival
earth: the traders' association must decide when the market runs, and your word now carries
scene: The market at {place} has grown, and the stalls no longer agree on when to open or close. Some want the early trade, some the late, and the people who live round the square want their evenings quiet. The association meets, and everyone turns to {N}.
- W | one set of hours for every stall, posted and kept by all | v: conformity, universalism | scope: town_sphere | chance: 70
- B | let each trader set their own hours and keep what they earn | v: achievement, power | scope: town_sphere | chance: 70
- R | open late on summer nights, with music, and see who comes | v: stimulation, hedonism | scope: place | chance: 60
- G | keep the market days the town has always had | v: tradition, security | scope: town_sphere | chance: 75
works: Within a season the new way at {place} feels as if it was always so, and the square is busy.
works: The traders who argued hardest at the meeting are the first to say it was the right call.
fails: Half the stalls ignore the decision, and the square is a muddle of open and shut for months.
fails: The neighbours and a handful of traders go to the council about it, and the quarrel drags on.

