works: The staff at {place} take the new terms better than {N} feared, and the shop comes through the year.
works: By the next year's end the books are steadier, and the decision is spoken of as the turning point.
fails: Two of the best hands leave for other shops, and {place} is short-staffed through the winter.
fails: The takings keep falling, and the decision is blamed for more than it did.

