earth: the town's credit union must decide who it lends to, and you sit at the head of its board
scene: The credit union at {place} has more money to lend than in years, and more people asking for it. The board cannot agree on who should come first. Small traders, new firms and old families all have a claim, and {N} has the deciding word.
- U>B | test each plan carefully, and charge what the risk is worth | v: achievement, power | scope: town_sphere | chance: 65
- B | lend to the firms most likely to grow, and grow the fund with them | v: achievement, power | scope: town_sphere | chance: 65
- G | lend first to the families the town has known for years | v: tradition, benevolence | scope: town_sphere | chance: 70
works: The loans go out, and by the next spring there are new shutters going up along the high street.
